ProjectForum is an innovative web-based application that can help
you bring increased interaction, coordination and communication to
online or face-to-face workgroup projects, business teams and project
intranets.  Easy to learn and use, ProjectForum can be hosted on
Mac OS X, Windows, Linux and FreeBSD, while users need only a
standard web browser.

ProjectForum 2.5 offers new SSL support, providing the option of
using fully encrypted connections for situations where privacy
and security are paramount.  A number of smaller enhancements
and bug fixes are also included in the new release; these are also
included with CourseForum 2.5, which brings the same benefits
to online or face-to-face courses and student groups.

ProjectForum licenses are available starting from US$199, while
CourseForum licenses start at US$79.  Free versions of both
products can also be downloaded, and a hosting service is available.

For more information, to try our demo sites, or to download free or
evaluation versions, visit http://www.projectforum.com.

